			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Define IPC routing tier types for NodeDeferred support\n\nIntroduce the `TierIPCValue` type definition ('Mountain' | 'NodeDeferred' | 'Node') in Source/Utility/Tier.ts to support the new three-tier IPC routing strategy. This typology enables the `ResolveInvoke` mechanism to selectively fallback to the Cocoon Node.js runtime when Tauri handlers are unavailable, as introduced in the recent IPC routing commits.\n\nThis change formalizes the configuration options for the `TierIPC` environment variable, ensuring type safety when selecting between direct Tauri invocation, deferred Node fallback, or direct Node routing.",
			"SHA": "a244b175fffd281dbc290851089b7a641cc9e878"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T00:37:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1939,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Implement NodeDeferred IPC routing and expand workspace/debug channel catalog\n\nExtended the IPC subsystem to support a new `NodeDeferred` routing tier, enabling seamless fallback to the Cocoon Node.js runtime when Mountain/Tauri handlers are unavailable. This introduces a three-tier configuration via the `TierIPC` environment variable:\n- `Mountain` (default): Direct invocation via Tauri.\n- `NodeDeferred`: Attempt Tauri first; on failure, forward requests to the Cocoon Node.js extension host via the `cocoon:request` bridge.\n- `Node`: Route all traffic directly to Cocoon, bypassing the Tauri layer.\n\nImplemented the `_InvokeViaNode` helper to facilitate relay calls through Mountain's gRPC bridge, ensuring compatibility with `__TAURI__` and `__TAURI_INTERNALS__` globals.\n\nAdditionally, updated the IPC channel catalog (`Source/IPC/Channel.ts`) with 20+ new stub channels covering workspace lifecycle events, storage operations, language features, SCM controls, debugging sessions, task execution, and authentication management. Standardized logging in `Source/Preload.ts` to use `_PreloadShimLog` instead of `console.warn` to reduce noise, and updated `ConfigurationImplementation.ts` to utilize `DevLog` for error reporting.",
			"SHA": "ede96ed63fcbba52010dfb85eaff36d379b2e422"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T23:38:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1939,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Add polling loop for Tauri IPC bridge initialization\n\nThe `ResolveConfiguration` function previously assumed the Tauri IPC globals (`__TAURI_INTERNALS__` or `__TAURI__`) were immediately available. In certain webview load orderings or with the specific Mountain fork, these globals may be undefined during initial module evaluation, causing the configuration fetch to fail prematurely.\n\nIntroduce a 5-second polling loop with a 25ms interval that retries detection of the `Invoke` function. If the IPC bridge remains unavailable after the deadline, log a diagnostic message via `DevLog` and proceed with default path fallbacks. This ensures the workbench can boot in degraded mode rather than stalling indefinitely during initialization, while still attempting to recover native functionality if the bridge becomes ready shortly after start.\n\nThe update refactors the IPC resolution logic into a reusable `ResolveInvoke` helper and wraps the invocation with explicit TypeScript casting to satisfy the type checker.",
			"SHA": "ca4b721dc89fe3ab21da124d09dd57aa980c36db"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T22:50:06Z",
			"File": [
